# Page acceptance contract

Full detail in `docs/page-acceptance-checklist.md`. Satisfy all of it before
returning a page, post or template change.

## Non negotiable

- **Robots:** `index, follow` for real content, `noindex, follow` for genuine
  placeholders. Never emit `nofollow` on our own pages, not even on a stub.
- **Canonical:** self referencing, bare domain (`https://allwebsites.design`),
  from `metadataBase`. Never a `www` URL.
- **Metadata:** build it with `pageMeta()` from `lib/seo.ts`. Do not hand roll a
  `Metadata` object. Descriptions must land in 150 to 165 characters; use
  `fitDescription()` when the text is generated.
- **One H1** in plain words. H2s phrased as the questions people type.
- **Answer block:** the first paragraph under the H1 is a self contained 40 to
  60 word answer that makes sense quoted alone.
- **Schema describes only what is visible.** If you emit `FAQPage`, every
  question and answer must be rendered on the page. This is checked.

## Statistics

Never write a number into prose. Compute it in `lib/insights.ts` from the
canonical record set and interpolate it, and surface its sample size next to it.
If a figure cannot be derived from `content/sites/*.json`, leave it out.

## Dates

Use `recordDates()` and respect its `exact` flag. When it is false the date
belongs to the archive release, not to a per record check, and the page must say
"Archive revision" rather than "Last checked". Never invent a timestamp.

## Adding a journal post

1. Add the entry to `JOURNAL` in `lib/journal.ts`: slug, title, h1, description,
   answer, `keyStat`, 3 to 5 `faqs`, 5 to 10 `fanout` questions, dates, status.
2. Add the body at `content/journal/<slug>.tsx` using the parts in
   `components/journal/ArticleParts.tsx`, including a `Method` block that states
   how each number was produced and a `Related` block with at least three links.
3. Register the body in `content/journal/index.ts`.
4. Sitemap, site map, footer and `llms.txt` pick it up automatically. Drafts are
   excluded from the sitemap because they carry `noindex`.

## Before returning

Run the gate and fix every failure:

```bash
npm run build && npm start -- -p 4360 &
npm run seo:check -- --base http://localhost:4360 --all
```

Do not use the em dash character in generated page copy.
